{"title":"1994 AHSME Problems/Problem 27","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A bag of popping corn contains <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/4/7547747b133453d3c209cff6cfbf129aa67a6947.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> white kernels and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> yellow kernels. Only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of the white kernels will pop, whereas <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/4/7547747b133453d3c209cff6cfbf129aa67a6947.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of the yellow ones will pop. A kernel is selected at random from the bag, and pops when placed in the popper. What is the probability that the kernel selected was white?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/5/83503f3e6d29db0fff3e39745ba1e7a061a0ef56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{5}{9} \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{4}{7} \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{3}{5} \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"367\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To find the probability that the kernel is white, the probability of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/4/e14ad566de6f9f23d3194d96eabd964633762d3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(\\mathrm{white|popped}) = \\frac{P(\\mathrm{white, popped})}{P(\\mathrm{popped})}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"300\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p>Running a bit of calculations <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/2/522b77992dfd049ce061f92f6adbee1d3eeb58a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(\\mathrm{white, popped}) = \\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"174\" height=\"37\" /> while <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/d/69dae3e366853a10c212dcaf606dd385514a233c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(\\mathrm{popped}) = \\frac{1}{3} + \\frac{2}{9} = \\frac{5}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"195\" height=\"37\" />. Plugging this into the earlier equation, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/e/6ae6a496ef2a78f441505e7bd1f77ae339352b11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(\\mathrm{white|popped}) = \\frac{\\frac{1}{3}}{\\frac{5}{9}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"172\" height=\"47\" />, meaning that the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/effc939e752c386097fcb31976223fb6f8356906.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{3}{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"59\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AHSME\" title=\"1994 AHSME\">1994 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1994 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1994 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1994\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26\" title=\"1994 AHSME Problems/Problem 26\">Problem 26</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28\" title=\"1994 AHSME Problems/Problem 28\">Problem 28</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1994 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1994 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1994 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1994 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1994 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1994 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1994 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AHSME_Pr